<capabilities>
<p>The Duat is an 8,500-ton military spheroid DropShip built around a single purpose: delivering and sustaining a combined force of BattleMechs and battle armor far from friendly support. Six BattleMech cubicles and bays for six battle armor units are backed by six oversize holds, later adapted to accept super-heavy 'Mechs, along with a foot infantry platoon for landing zone security and several hundred tons of additional cargo space. A drone carrier control system allows the Duat to field six Celerity or Revenant drones, extending its reconnaissance reach well beyond the landing zone. Three nose-mounted cruise missile launchers give the vessel genuine artillery capability, while batteries of Gauss rifles, Artemis-guided multi-missile launchers, and large variable-speed pulse lasers cover the nose, flanks, and aft. Laser anti-missile systems guard the forward quarters and the aft arc, and ninety-seven tons of heavy ferro-aluminum armor provide sound protection for a transport. The Duat's weaknesses lie in its modest thrust, which leaves it unable to outrun most combat DropShips, and in the heavy ammunition demands of its missile and Gauss batteries, which tie the vessel closely to its supply chain.</p>
</capabilities>

<overview>
<p>The Duat is a military transport DropShip designed and built in secret by a renegade Blessed Order faction of ComStar to carry and supply the secret Com Guard formations that persisted within Republic space during the Dark Age. Introduced in 3131 and produced at New Earth, the design was intended to deliver a Level II of BattleMechs and a Level II of battle armor, together with the supplies needed to keep them in the field, wherever the Com Guards' hidden war required them. For years the Republic Armed Forces had no reliable intelligence that such a vessel existed at all. Those Duats that have since come into Republic hands are regarded as some of the most advanced transports in the RAF, prized by the raiding teams that operate beyond the Fortress Wall, though the class's ComStar origins have left it with a lingering reputation that commanders outside the Republic are slow to forget.</p>
</overview>

<deployment>
<p>The standard Duat serves in its baseline transport configuration, carrying combined BattleMech, battle armor, and drone forces on raids beyond the Fortress Wall for the Republic Armed Forces. A typical operation sees a pair of Duats land a raiding force under a battle armor screen, after which drone operators aboard the DropShips scout the surrounding terrain and call in cruise missile strikes on any target their drones uncover. Because the class was designed and built by ComStar, no Inner Sphere power identifies a Duat as a Republic asset, which makes the vessels especially well suited to covert missions. The most experienced crews have become adept at using their drones as artillery spotters, and RAF planners have studied their methods closely.</p>
</deployment>

<history>
<p>A renegade Blessed Order faction within ComStar developed the Duat in secret during the early thirty-second century, as part of its effort to rebuild the Com Guards and support the formations it continued to maintain within Republic territory. Built at New Earth and introduced in 3131, the class was designed around the Com Guards' own organization, carrying the Level IIs of BattleMechs and battle armor on which those forces were built. Alongside the Kheper and Uraeus BattleMechs, the Duat proved that ComStar's military reach was far greater than Republic intelligence had believed, and confirmation of the vessel's existence and specifications after Fortress Republic was raised provoked serious recriminations within the RAF's intelligence services.</p><p>Eliminating the rogue Com Guard became one of the RAF's most important efforts behind the Wall, and the Duat proved a dangerous opponent. During the campaign against the First Division on Epsilon Eridani, the division's Duats struck the advancing Republic forces with salvo after salvo of cruise missiles, breaking their formations again and again. Some strategists have credited this bombardment with forcing the Hastati Sentinels into a combat drop.</p><p>With the Com Guard defeated, the few captured Duats, joined by vessels delivered from the New Earth Trading Company, entered RAF service, where they became prized assets for raiding teams operating across the Fortress Wall. Later vessels were refitted to carry the Ares and Poseidon super-heavy 'Mechs of the Rhodes Project, further increasing the class's value. In early 3145, a pair of Duats landed a force of Poseidon tripods and drones on Small World, combining drone reconnaissance with cruise missile fire to throw the Draconis Combine garrison into disarray. As the DropShips withdrew, a squadron of Combine Shilone fighters attempted to cripple them with long-range missile fire, only to see the Duats' aft anti-missile systems stop nearly every missile while their Gauss rifles struck back. Duats have since been entrusted with some of the most sensitive duties in the Republic, including transport for the personal guard of Devlin Stone, and in 3149 several Duats carried Republic troops to Calloway.</p>
</history>

